      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the scene of men in Islamic attire discussing goat meat",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the bottom scene (the men in traditional Islamic attire) as the implied audience or subject of the stereotype being presented. The meme does not contain explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing positions the viewer as an external observer who is being invited to accept or react to the stereotype about Islamic countries consuming goat meat. The projection is onto the scene of the men, who are the visual representation of the 'Islamic countries' being stereotyped, making the user perceive themselves as part of the judgment or commentary on that stereotype.",
